Bridge 0128 (G7): the GPU YCbCr path converted a texture's planes at every encoder that used it (backboardd ~2 full-frame conversions per
CA frame, ~45 ms GPU each: 1080p video at ~10 fps). (1) Seed gating: the frontend hands a converted texture its IOSurface's seed source
(nmb_texture_watch_seed); ShadowSync::before skips the conversion while IOSurfaceGetSeed and 0116's write stamp (commands writing the
planes, deferred work) are unchanged since the last planned conversion; views share the texture's seed. Like 0112's planarFill, ours (AdrenoMetal
had no seed cache in its frontend). Off: SWEET_YCBCR_SEED=0 (needs M2V_SHADOW_CACHE on for the stamp). (2) The conversion kernel with the
texture's 22 shape words baked in as constants (one pipeline per shape, at most 8 a process; decoder pools share one): no shape SSBO loads
per texel, and the code layout's udiv/imul/shift by 1 and 0 fold away. Off: SWEET_YCBCR_BAKE=0. Image format unchanged (RGBA16F).
SHADOW: line gains "ycbcr converted N seed-skipped M".

